<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16961" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀτά̆ρ-ακτος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>not disturbed, uniform,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περίοδοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Ti.</u>
					47c
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>not disturbed, without confusion, steady,</i> of soldiers,
				<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				2.1.31
			</span></i>: generally, <i>quiet,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Eq.</u>
				7.10
			</span></i>(
				Sup.
			). Adv.
			
				Sup.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ότατα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Eq.Mag.</u>
					2.1
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>not excited, calm,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				630b12
			</span></i>: 
				Comp.
			, <i><span class="en">
				M.Ant.
				4.24
			</span></i>; of the sea, prob. in <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				944b23
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τως, ζῆν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>Herc.</u>
					1003
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
